  "description": "Ed25519 strict-verification negative vector (RFC-ACDP-0001 \u00a75.10, acdp-rs#342). A signature whose public key A and nonce point R are small-order satisfies the cofactorless verification equation [s]B = R + [k]A for EVERY message, so a non-strict verifier (e.g. ed25519-dalek `verify`, OpenSSL) accepts it. A conformant verifier MUST reject it with invalid_signature. The runner checks the arithmetic (equation holds, A and R are small-order); the rejection itself is verified by implementations.",
